  "source": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/LXIII/653/653-10.htm",
  "statuteText": "653:10 Assumption of Office. –\n\nFederal officers-elect shall assume office on the date set by the U.S. Constitution. State officers-elect shall assume office on the date set by the New Hampshire Constitution. County officers-elect shall assume office on the first Wednesday after the first Tuesday in January of the year following the state general election at which they were elected."
